WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.030
Only about one in ten people in
Rwanda had electricity in 2010.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.690
By 2024, it was about seven in ten.

3
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.890
Solar panels now sit on rural rooftops.

4
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:20.750
Child deaths fell too: from 184 per
1,000 live births in 2000 to 38 in 2024.

5
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.570
Some change is planned
and run by government.

6
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.270
Some works directly with local people.

7
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.590
So which works better?

8
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.070
Do national plans always
reach everyone faster?

9
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.770
In this mission, you'll measure Rwanda's
progress towards three of the UN's 17

10
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.190
Sustainable Development Goals.

11
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.670
Then you'll compare one top-down
and one bottom-up strategy,

12
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.010
and weigh the strengths of each.

13
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.930
Your mission: decide whether national
plans beat village-level projects.
